M158's patch 0037 drew this line through ui/gfx once and two files were on
the other side of it. The sentence is M144's and it has not changed: being
in the Linux family is not having Linux's kernel.

  gpu_fence.cc            sync_wait(2) and sync_file_info(3), which are
                          third_party/libsync over Linux's sync_file ioctls.
                          The #else branch every one of these three blocks
                          already has is NOTREACHED(), which is the right
                          answer on a machine with no GPU to hand out a
                          fence in the first place.

  ui/gfx/BUILD.gn         and therefore the //third_party/libsync dependency
  ui/gl/BUILD.gn          itself, whose sync.c includes <linux/sync_file.h>.
                          Two directories depend on it and gating one left
                          ninja building it for the other, which is worth
                          saying: a dependency removed is only removed when
                          the last edge to it is. ui/gl's own comment beside
                          that block already excludes Fuchsia "due to a
                          libsync dependency" - the same reason, one platform
                          earlier. What the sources there implement is
                          EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync, a fence a GPU driver
                          hands out, so there is no second use for them here.

  native_pixmap_handle.cc <drm_fourcc.h>, which is Linux's DRM format
                          numbering - the kernel's uapi header, of which
                          libdrm ships a copy. This one is narrower than the
                          others on purpose: the only thing the file wants
                          from that header is DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID for a
                          static_assert, and the plane file descriptors
                          around it are ordinary descriptors. Widening the
                          guard to the whole block would take the struct's
                          own fields with it, and those are declared under
                          the same condition in the HEADER - where the #else
                          is "#error Unsupported OS".

HAS_LINUX_KERNEL is M144's buildflag and IS_LINUX is Chromium's own. Neither
this patch nor 0037 nor 0038 mentions any operating system by name.

diff --git a/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn b/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn
--- a/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn
+++ b/ui/gfx/BUILD.gn
@@ -644,7 +644,11 @@
     deps += [ "//build/config/linux/libdrm" ]
   }
 
-  if (is_linux || is_chromeos || is_android) {
+  # libsync is Android's wrapper over Linux's sync_file ioctls and its sync.c
+  # includes <linux/sync_file.h>. Same sentence as the block above: which
+  # family the build gates a platform as does not decide whether Linux's
+  # kernel interfaces are there.
+  if ((is_linux || is_chromeos || is_android) && has_linux_kernel) {
     deps += [ "//third_party/libsync" ]
   }
 
